## 8. Interface Contracts for Downstream Milestones

### 8.1 Integration with `server/index.js` (Milestone 1, Explorer M1.3)
When `GET /api/stream` is requested, `server/index.js` invokes `resolveStream`:

```javascript
const resolver = require('./resolver');

// GET /api/stream?tmdbId=27205&type=movie&server=secret
app.get('/api/stream', async (req, res) => {
  try {
    const { tmdbId, type, season, episode, server } = req.query;
    const result = await resolver.resolveStream({ tmdbId, type, season, episode, server });

    // Construct local proxied stream URL
    const proxyStreamUrl = `http://${req.headers.host || '127.0.0.1:8088'}/hls/proxy?url=${encodeURIComponent(result.originalUrl)}`;

    res.json({
      success: true,
      streamUrl: proxyStreamUrl,
      originalUrl: result.originalUrl,
      server: result.server,
      captions: result.captions
    });
  } catch (err) {
    res.status(500).json({ success: false, error: err.message });
  }
});
```

### 8.2 Integration with `server/hls-proxy.js` (Milestone 1, Explorer M1.2)
The `originalUrl` returned from `resolveStream` is passed directly into `/hls/proxy?url=...` for manifest rewriting and segment streaming with injected `Origin: https://cinejoy.pk`.

